## Requirements

- [Devbox](https://www.jetify.com/devbox) for support tools (just, pnpm, Postgres…).
- Node (version in `.node-version`, e.g. via `fnm`).
{%- if backend == 'go' %}
- Go (version in `apps/api/go.mod`).
{%- else %}
- Rust via `rustup` (version in `apps/api/rust-toolchain.toml`).
{%- endif %}
- Xcode / Android Studio for native development builds.

## Getting started

```bash
devbox shell
just setup        # install, generate, start local Postgres
just dev-api      # API on http://localhost:8080
just dev-app      # Expo dev server
just verify       # everything CI runs
```

Run `just` to list every recipe.
{%- if mobile_builds == 'local' %}

## App builds

Builds are local; no Expo account or EAS is involved. Set `APP_API_URL` in `.env` to
the dev API's public URL (it is baked into release builds), then:

```bash
just app-ios "iPhone 17 Pro"   # release build on a simulator or a connected iPhone
just app-ios-xcode             # open the native project in Xcode (Product → Archive for TestFlight)
just app-android               # release build on a device or emulator (Android Studio)
just app-web                   # static export into apps/app/dist
```

iOS needs Xcode and CocoaPods (`brew install cocoapods`). `apps/app/ios` and
`apps/app/android` are generated by `expo prebuild` and stay out of git. There is no mobile CI
and there are no over-the-air updates: every change tested on a phone is a new build.
{%- endif %}

## Agent commits

Agents commit as `{{ agent_name }} <{{ agent_email }}>`, you commit as yourself. In a task
worktree, `just agent-identity <model> <task>` sets that identity and a `commit-msg` hook that
adds `Agent-Model:` and `Agent-Task:` trailers, whichever model drives the agent. Merge PRs
with a merge commit (squash and rebase are disabled by `scripts/github-bootstrap.sh`), so
`git blame` keeps agent and human lines apart. To see who wrote what:

```bash
git log --author='{{ agent_name }}' --format='%h %s %(trailers:key=Agent-Model,valueonly,separator=)'
```

Generated from [pscaffold](https://github.com/askhari/pscaffold). The `template-update`
workflow opens a pull request every week when a new template release is out; to update by
hand, run `devbox run -- copier update --trust`, then `devbox run -- just setup`.
